WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.921 --> 00:00:04.230
- [Narrator] Imagine a
small rural village in Iraq

00:00:04.230 --> 00:00:07.710
in the middle of the night in 2003.

00:00:07.710 --> 00:00:10.395
A man is hiding inside
an underground hole.

00:00:10.395 --> 00:00:13.513
Its entrance covered with styrofoam.

00:00:13.513 --> 00:00:17.430
And suddenly, the streetlights
in the entire village go out

00:00:17.430 --> 00:00:19.320
and hundreds of U.S. soldiers

00:00:19.320 --> 00:00:22.020
begin sweeping through the town.

00:00:22.020 --> 00:00:24.046
As the troops reach the farmhouse,

00:00:24.046 --> 00:00:26.521
a soldier starts to unearth a rope,

00:00:26.521 --> 00:00:30.200
discovering that it leads
to the hidden trap door.

00:00:30.200 --> 00:00:34.410
They open it and prepare to
throw a grenade into the hole

00:00:34.410 --> 00:00:36.150
just to be safe.

00:00:36.150 --> 00:00:37.968
But just before the pin is pulled,

00:00:37.968 --> 00:00:42.510
everyone freezes as a pair of
hands emerge from the hole,

00:00:42.510 --> 00:00:45.450
followed by a bearded man.

00:00:45.450 --> 00:00:49.297
With his hands in the air, he
declares to those around him.

00:00:49.297 --> 00:00:51.516
"My name is Saddam Hussein.

00:00:51.516 --> 00:00:56.100
I am the president of Iraq
and I want to negotiate."

00:00:56.100 --> 00:00:58.997
- Ladies and gentlemen, we got him.

00:00:58.997 --> 00:01:00.540
(gentle music)

00:01:00.540 --> 00:01:02.160
- [Narrator] Whether
you've heard the story

00:01:02.160 --> 00:01:03.420
of Saddam's hiding place

00:01:03.420 --> 00:01:06.090
because of the countless
memes circulating online,

00:01:06.090 --> 00:01:08.190
or whether you lived through this time

00:01:08.190 --> 00:01:09.870
and think you remember it,

00:01:09.870 --> 00:01:12.521
I doubt you ever heard the full story.

00:01:12.521 --> 00:01:17.004
And so for this video, I
will be exploring just that.

00:01:17.004 --> 00:01:20.283
This is how Saddam Hussein was found.

00:01:21.400 --> 00:01:23.310
(dramatic music)

00:01:23.310 --> 00:01:26.250
The hunt for Saddam began
with the invasion of Iraq

00:01:26.250 --> 00:01:27.990
in March of 2003.

00:01:27.990 --> 00:01:30.330
- My fellow citizens, at this hour,

00:01:30.330 --> 00:01:33.210
American and coalition forces
are in the early stages

00:01:33.210 --> 00:01:37.560
of military operations to
disarm Iraq, to free its people,

00:01:37.560 --> 00:01:40.080
and to defend the world from grave danger.

00:01:40.080 --> 00:01:42.090
- [Narrator] The U.S.
had started a coalition

00:01:42.090 --> 00:01:44.050
to overthrow the Iraqi president,

00:01:44.050 --> 00:01:47.460
and the reason they presented
to the world for doing so

00:01:47.460 --> 00:01:48.900
was that they claimed Saddam

00:01:48.900 --> 00:01:51.300
was hiding weapons of mass destruction.

00:01:51.300 --> 00:01:54.630
- There is no doubt that Saddam Hussein

00:01:54.630 --> 00:01:57.690
now has weapons of mass destruction.

00:01:57.690 --> 00:02:00.840
- [Narrator] A claim that would
later turn out to be false.

00:02:00.840 --> 00:02:01.830
- You know, when we first got in there

00:02:01.830 --> 00:02:03.666
and started looking around
and didn't find anything,

00:02:03.666 --> 00:02:06.313
get that kinda sinking feeling that uh-oh.

00:02:07.362 --> 00:02:08.933
(suspenseful music)

00:02:08.933 --> 00:02:11.340
- [Narrator] The invasion itself went fast

00:02:11.340 --> 00:02:13.340
as the United States, along
with troops from the U.K.,

00:02:13.340 --> 00:02:16.080
Australia, and Poland fought their way

00:02:16.080 --> 00:02:17.940
to the capital city of Baghdad,

00:02:17.940 --> 00:02:21.810
which fell just three weeks
after the initial invasion.

00:02:21.810 --> 00:02:23.610
But still, the troops were not able

00:02:23.610 --> 00:02:26.220
to find the Iraqi
president, Saddam Hussein.

00:02:26.220 --> 00:02:28.200
- [Reporter] To the very heart of Baghdad,

00:02:28.200 --> 00:02:30.452
U.S. tanks and troops finally arrive,

00:02:30.452 --> 00:02:33.300
spelling the end for the Iraqi regime.

00:02:33.300 --> 00:02:35.550
The next task, to hunt down the men

00:02:35.550 --> 00:02:38.880
who fought and defended
the city for a fortnight.

00:02:38.880 --> 00:02:39.750
- [Narrator] And in the middle

00:02:39.750 --> 00:02:41.760
of a public square in the city,

00:02:41.760 --> 00:02:45.624
American forces join Iraqis
near a massive statue

00:02:45.624 --> 00:02:49.124
dedicated to Saddam, whose
rule has come to an end.

00:02:49.124 --> 00:02:51.480
And to declare their victory,

00:02:51.480 --> 00:02:54.240
American soldiers placed an American flag

00:02:54.240 --> 00:02:56.353
over the face of the statue.

00:02:56.353 --> 00:02:59.730
This was much to the dismay
of the Iraqi citizens

00:02:59.730 --> 00:03:02.630
who had gathered with them,
as raising an American flag

00:03:02.630 --> 00:03:07.560
seemed to represent the U.S.
controlling the Iraqi people.

00:03:07.560 --> 00:03:10.050
And after realizing
the image this created,

00:03:10.050 --> 00:03:14.280
the soldiers quickly replaced
their flag with an Iraqi one,

00:03:14.280 --> 00:03:16.853
and then the statue was toppled.

00:03:16.853 --> 00:03:19.620
(crowd cheering)

00:03:19.620 --> 00:03:22.020
But though his likeness
was brought to the ground,

00:03:22.020 --> 00:03:24.363
the real Saddam was still at large.

00:03:25.230 --> 00:03:28.282
Locating him and other high
ranking members of his regime

00:03:28.282 --> 00:03:31.890
became a top priority
for the U.S. military.

00:03:31.890 --> 00:03:34.530
And to keep track of the
targeted former officials,

00:03:34.530 --> 00:03:37.170
a special deck of playing cards is created

00:03:37.170 --> 00:03:40.911
that features the 52
most wanted officials.

00:03:40.911 --> 00:03:44.191
This way, soldiers who regularly
play games during breaks

00:03:44.191 --> 00:03:46.577
will be able to easily
pick up high value targets

00:03:46.577 --> 00:03:50.400
and recognize the faces
of those on the hunt.

00:03:50.400 --> 00:03:53.550
And Saddam Hussein remains
priority number one,

00:03:53.550 --> 00:03:57.750
the Ace of Spades, along
with his sons, Uday and Qusay

00:03:57.750 --> 00:03:58.922
right below him.

00:03:58.922 --> 00:04:01.020
- [Reporter] In the
skies and on the ground

00:04:01.020 --> 00:04:03.960
they have one order, to find Saddam.

00:04:03.960 --> 00:04:06.090
The word is he never stays in one place

00:04:06.090 --> 00:04:07.380
for more than a few hours,

00:04:07.380 --> 00:04:10.980
constantly on the move probably by car.

00:04:10.980 --> 00:04:14.040
- [Narrator] Several months
pass after the fall of Baghdad.

00:04:14.040 --> 00:04:17.280
And many targets are
found and apprehended,

00:04:17.280 --> 00:04:18.720
but none of them lead the U.S.

00:04:18.720 --> 00:04:21.840
to where Saddam or his sons are hiding.

00:04:21.840 --> 00:04:23.326
To gather more information,

00:04:23.326 --> 00:04:27.840
a $15 million bounty was
placed on each brother,

00:04:27.840 --> 00:04:31.590
and a $25 million bounty
was put forth for Saddam.

00:04:31.590 --> 00:04:35.970
- Senator, is today's $25
million on the head of Saddam

00:04:35.970 --> 00:04:37.350
gonna change anything?

00:04:37.350 --> 00:04:39.930
- [Reporter] With a reward of $25 million,

00:04:39.930 --> 00:04:42.600
American troops are increasingly confident

00:04:42.600 --> 00:04:46.140
that they will soon have
the ace in their pack.

00:04:46.140 --> 00:04:48.930
- [Narrator] And this incentive
gives the American military

00:04:48.930 --> 00:04:51.300
the exact break they had been looking for

00:04:51.300 --> 00:04:53.940
as four months after the start of the war,

00:04:53.940 --> 00:04:56.730
a man enters a military base in Mosul,

00:04:56.730 --> 00:05:01.403
claiming that he's sheltering
Uday and Qusay in his home.

00:05:01.403 --> 00:05:03.270
(suspenseful music)

00:05:03.270 --> 00:05:05.100
Almost unable to believe it,

00:05:05.100 --> 00:05:08.280
troops are dispatched the
next day to the man's house

00:05:08.280 --> 00:05:12.273
located in Mosul, the
second largest city of Iraq.

00:05:13.110 --> 00:05:16.601
And to their surprise,
Saddam's sons, Uday and Qusay

00:05:16.601 --> 00:05:20.217
are actually inside the
building, hiding in a mansion

00:05:20.217 --> 00:05:23.793
that is now being
surrounded by U.S. troops.

00:05:24.960 --> 00:05:28.170
And as the brothers are not
willing to come quietly,

00:05:28.170 --> 00:05:30.660
gunfire breaks out.

00:05:30.660 --> 00:05:34.710
The U.S. troops retreat
and call in reinforcements.

00:05:34.710 --> 00:05:37.320
Not only do they get additional manpower,

00:05:37.320 --> 00:05:39.986
but also a missile strike
is called on the house

00:05:39.986 --> 00:05:44.986
the brothers are hiding in,
destroying most of the house.

00:05:45.510 --> 00:05:47.009
And after the dust is cleared,

00:05:47.009 --> 00:05:49.462
soldiers are able to enter the house,

00:05:49.462 --> 00:05:53.100
but the brothers had already been killed.

00:05:53.100 --> 00:05:54.957
- Everybody agrees that
it would've been better

00:05:54.957 --> 00:05:57.636
if the brothers had been captured alive.

00:05:57.636 --> 00:05:59.670
- I would never consider this a failure.

00:05:59.670 --> 00:06:01.824
Our mission is to find, kill or capture.

00:06:01.824 --> 00:06:04.050
(gentle techno music)

00:06:04.050 --> 00:06:06.360
- [Narrator] Even though
it is perhaps unlikely

00:06:06.360 --> 00:06:09.150
his sons would've given any
information to the Americans

00:06:09.150 --> 00:06:12.570
about where Saddam is hiding,
with both of them gone,

00:06:12.570 --> 00:06:16.380
the road to finding him remains unclear.

00:06:16.380 --> 00:06:18.570
But what the raid on the safe house did

00:06:18.570 --> 00:06:23.284
is it triggered Saddam to
release a sign of life himself

00:06:23.284 --> 00:06:26.765
as an audio tape surfaces and is broadcast

00:06:26.765 --> 00:06:29.075
on which Saddam can be heard mourning

00:06:29.075 --> 00:06:30.720
the loss of his two sons.

00:06:30.720 --> 00:06:33.690
(Saddam speaking in foreign language)

00:06:33.690 --> 00:06:35.250
- [Narrator] The existence of this tape

00:06:35.250 --> 00:06:38.790
confirms that Saddam is still alive.

00:06:38.790 --> 00:06:40.830
And the other thing this
whole situation showed

00:06:40.830 --> 00:06:43.853
is that the bounty had resulted
in someone coming forward

00:06:43.853 --> 00:06:46.830
and providing helpful information.

00:06:46.830 --> 00:06:49.000
- Secretary Powell today
approved the payment

00:06:49.000 --> 00:06:52.529
of $30 million reward to the individual

00:06:52.529 --> 00:06:55.620
who provided the critical
piece of information.

00:06:55.620 --> 00:06:57.420
- [Narrator] Therefore, the U.S. decides

00:06:57.420 --> 00:06:59.966
to pay the full reward to the informant.

00:06:59.966 --> 00:07:04.320
$30 million in addition to being relocated

00:07:04.320 --> 00:07:06.210
to the United States.

00:07:06.210 --> 00:07:08.497
Their hope is that once Iraqi citizens

00:07:08.497 --> 00:07:12.030
see that the U.S. is serious
about their bounties,

00:07:12.030 --> 00:07:13.620
it would encourage more people

00:07:13.620 --> 00:07:16.020
to step forward with information.

00:07:16.020 --> 00:07:17.340
- We're trying to look for Saddam Hussein.

00:07:17.340 --> 00:07:19.980
We have his two sons and we
already took care of them,

00:07:19.980 --> 00:07:21.152
but we need Saddam Hussein.

00:07:21.152 --> 00:07:22.740
We're urging the Iraqi people

00:07:22.740 --> 00:07:24.510
to help us out any way that they can.

00:07:24.510 --> 00:07:26.640
- [Reporter] There's no
shortage of information.

00:07:26.640 --> 00:07:31.053
But with a $25 million reward
on offer, much is unreliable.

00:07:31.950 --> 00:07:33.420
- [Narrator] But as the months rolled by

00:07:33.420 --> 00:07:36.201
with many unsuccessful
raids to capture Saddam,

00:07:36.201 --> 00:07:39.044
it begins to seem less and less likely

00:07:39.044 --> 00:07:41.554
that anyone will come forward.

00:07:41.554 --> 00:07:43.770
(door thudding)

00:07:43.770 --> 00:07:45.300
- [Reporter 1] Three civilians were shot

00:07:45.300 --> 00:07:46.484
during last night's raid.

00:07:46.484 --> 00:07:49.920
Innocent victims of this frantic search.

00:07:49.920 --> 00:07:51.270
- [Reporter 2] An elite secretive unit

00:07:51.270 --> 00:07:53.760
known as Task Force 20
is leading the hunt.

00:07:53.760 --> 00:07:55.410
There is no clear indication tonight

00:07:55.410 --> 00:07:57.180
that his capture is imminent.

00:07:57.180 --> 00:08:00.690
- The Americans are not about
to apologize for all of this.

00:08:00.690 --> 00:08:02.887
- [Reporter 1] A trail of
destruction left in the wake

00:08:02.887 --> 00:08:04.517
of the special task force

00:08:04.517 --> 00:08:07.292
that's hunting down Saddam Hussein.

00:08:07.292 --> 00:08:10.170
(soft percussive music)

00:08:10.170 --> 00:08:11.310
- [Narrator] With many of the raids

00:08:11.310 --> 00:08:14.730
leading to absolutely nothing,
the focus again shifts.

00:08:14.730 --> 00:08:16.800
And the U.S. military puts their attention

00:08:16.800 --> 00:08:19.565
towards completing the
deck by tracking down

00:08:19.565 --> 00:08:23.207
prior officials from Saddam's regime.

00:08:23.207 --> 00:08:24.926
Several high ranking officials

00:08:24.926 --> 00:08:28.115
that worked directly
under Saddam were captured

00:08:28.115 --> 00:08:30.029
with the hope that they might be able

00:08:30.029 --> 00:08:32.739
to provide information.

00:08:32.739 --> 00:08:35.430
Surprisingly though,
none of them can point

00:08:35.430 --> 00:08:37.817
to their former president's hiding place.

00:08:37.817 --> 00:08:40.535
And while the bulk of the
military remained focused

00:08:40.535 --> 00:08:42.963
on hunting targets from the deck of cards,

00:08:42.963 --> 00:08:46.050
one Staff Sergeant Eric Maddox

00:08:46.050 --> 00:08:50.370
decides to go into a
completely different direction.

00:08:50.370 --> 00:08:53.400
Maddox realizes that the
targets they are focused on

00:08:53.400 --> 00:08:57.300
represent the old regime
that had fallen from power.

00:08:57.300 --> 00:08:59.284
These are people that were given positions

00:08:59.284 --> 00:09:01.860
because they were related to Saddam,

00:09:01.860 --> 00:09:05.340
and so their power came from him.

00:09:05.340 --> 00:09:07.740
Right now, what Saddam needs is people

00:09:07.740 --> 00:09:09.510
with the power to protect him,

00:09:09.510 --> 00:09:13.593
and that can only come from
one place, his bodyguards.

00:09:14.448 --> 00:09:18.299
While in power, Saddam had a
system of personal protection

00:09:18.299 --> 00:09:21.240
comprised of three different tiers.

00:09:21.240 --> 00:09:22.890
The outermost level of guards

00:09:22.890 --> 00:09:24.780
were assigned to fixed locations,

00:09:24.780 --> 00:09:28.440
such as his various
palaces across the country.

00:09:28.440 --> 00:09:30.367
Above them was a level of guards

00:09:30.367 --> 00:09:32.610
that would travel ahead of Saddam

00:09:32.610 --> 00:09:36.301
to secure locations in various areas.

00:09:36.301 --> 00:09:39.956
And finally, above these
guards were the Hamaya,

00:09:39.956 --> 00:09:42.712
the innermost layer of elite guards.

00:09:42.712 --> 00:09:46.593
Those who would stay
with Saddam at all times.

00:09:47.760 --> 00:09:50.070
Maddox theorizes that these guards

00:09:50.070 --> 00:09:52.980
are likely the ones
currently protecting Saddam.

00:09:52.980 --> 00:09:54.420
And in order to find them,

00:09:54.420 --> 00:09:58.173
he begins his work in
Tikrit, Saddam's hometown.

00:09:59.520 --> 00:10:02.040
Tikrit had already been
thoroughly searched

00:10:02.040 --> 00:10:05.553
and it is largely believed
that Saddam isn't hiding here.

00:10:06.600 --> 00:10:08.392
However, it is still a hotbed

00:10:08.392 --> 00:10:12.750
for another family group, the Al-Muslit.

00:10:12.750 --> 00:10:14.762
And most of Saddam's elite bodyguards

00:10:14.762 --> 00:10:18.510
came from exactly this family.

00:10:18.510 --> 00:10:20.970
As Maddox begins his interrogations,

00:10:20.970 --> 00:10:24.120
he notices that one name keeps popping up.

00:10:24.120 --> 00:10:27.480
Muhammad Ibrahim Omar Al-Muslit.

00:10:27.480 --> 00:10:30.270
And the more Maddox learns
about Muhammad Ibrahim,

00:10:30.270 --> 00:10:34.221
the more convinced he feels
that he is on the right track.

00:10:34.221 --> 00:10:36.384
Not only was Muhammad Ibrahim

00:10:36.384 --> 00:10:40.080
one of Saddam's most trusted
inner circle bodyguards,

00:10:40.080 --> 00:10:42.630
but it seems like he is currently leading

00:10:42.630 --> 00:10:46.620
the entire resistance
against the U.S. occupation.

00:10:46.620 --> 00:10:48.570
He had installed several lieutenants

00:10:48.570 --> 00:10:50.790
in charge of certain areas of Iraq

00:10:50.790 --> 00:10:54.090
to coordinate attacks
against coalition forces.

00:10:54.090 --> 00:10:58.320
And he is the one coordinating
funds for counter attacks.

00:10:58.320 --> 00:10:59.820
- [Reporter] Saddam's loyalists here

00:10:59.820 --> 00:11:01.740
had taken off their uniforms

00:11:01.740 --> 00:11:04.796
and tried to fight the
Marines with guerilla tactics.

00:11:04.796 --> 00:11:06.630
- [Narrator] And if Muhammad Ibrahim

00:11:06.630 --> 00:11:09.269
is really running operations
in Saddam's stead,

00:11:09.269 --> 00:11:13.260
then he has to know
where Saddam is hiding.

00:11:13.260 --> 00:11:17.073
And so, Muhammad Ibrahim
becomes a prime target.

00:11:18.767 --> 00:11:21.094
To get to him, Maddox Interrogates

00:11:21.094 --> 00:11:23.940
a nephew of Muhammad Ibrahim,

00:11:23.940 --> 00:11:26.081
who then reveals the names and locations

00:11:26.081 --> 00:11:28.920
of two close business associates,

00:11:28.920 --> 00:11:33.480
as well as the name of
Muhammad's driver, Basim Latif.

00:11:33.480 --> 00:11:35.477
Basim along with family members

00:11:35.477 --> 00:11:38.820
of these business
associates are interrogated

00:11:38.820 --> 00:11:41.790
and the U.S. is able to
begin filling in the gaps

00:11:41.790 --> 00:11:43.860
of Muhammad's movement.

00:11:43.860 --> 00:11:46.080
So far that they even find out

00:11:46.080 --> 00:11:49.050
the location of Muhammad's son, Muslit,

00:11:49.050 --> 00:11:51.093
who is interrogated next.

00:11:52.140 --> 00:11:54.090
Initially, it seems that Muslit

00:11:54.090 --> 00:11:56.310
isn't able to be of much help.

00:11:56.310 --> 00:11:59.064
He didn't have much
involvement in the resistance,

00:11:59.064 --> 00:12:00.561
but what he did reveal

00:12:00.561 --> 00:12:04.440
is that he used to often
go fishing with his father.

00:12:04.440 --> 00:12:06.110
And even though they don't go anymore,

00:12:06.110 --> 00:12:08.667
he knows that his father still fishes

00:12:08.667 --> 00:12:11.793
at a pond he owns in the city of Samarra.

00:12:12.810 --> 00:12:15.720
This may seem like a trivial
piece of information,

00:12:15.720 --> 00:12:19.155
but Maddox thought back to an
interrogation he had before

00:12:19.155 --> 00:12:22.650
with a prior housekeeper of Saddam.

00:12:22.650 --> 00:12:24.450
He remembers that the housekeeper

00:12:24.450 --> 00:12:27.540
had mentioned that Saddam loved Masgouf,

00:12:27.540 --> 00:12:30.720
a type of fish that is popular in Iraq.

00:12:30.720 --> 00:12:33.189
Suddenly, the trail seemed red hot

00:12:33.189 --> 00:12:35.718
and Maddox was certain that Muhammad

00:12:35.718 --> 00:12:39.045
would be able to lead him to Saddam.

00:12:39.045 --> 00:12:41.220
(bright lilting music)

00:12:41.220 --> 00:12:44.545
To find out more, U.S.
forces raid the fish farm

00:12:44.545 --> 00:12:47.100
Muhammad was known to use.

00:12:47.100 --> 00:12:48.463
Two fishermen were located,

00:12:48.463 --> 00:12:51.199
but neither of them were Muhammad.

00:12:51.199 --> 00:12:53.730
And when these fishermen are questioned,

00:12:53.730 --> 00:12:56.682
Maddox finds out that
one of them was a cousin

00:12:56.682 --> 00:12:59.610
to a lieutenant in the resistance.

00:12:59.610 --> 00:13:03.060
And the fisherman also
mentions an uncle they shared

00:13:03.060 --> 00:13:05.673
who had a house in Baghdad.

00:13:05.673 --> 00:13:09.333
Perhaps Muhammad could be hiding there.

00:13:10.620 --> 00:13:13.048
If so, he would be hiding in plain sight

00:13:13.048 --> 00:13:15.780
in the Iraqi capital of Baghdad

00:13:15.780 --> 00:13:17.460
that had been under the control

00:13:17.460 --> 00:13:20.700
of the U.S. led coalition for months.

00:13:20.700 --> 00:13:22.650
But with no better lead to follow,

00:13:22.650 --> 00:13:26.181
the decision is made to
raid the house in Baghdad.

00:13:26.181 --> 00:13:28.410
When you think about it,

00:13:28.410 --> 00:13:32.100
what led them here is a
series of rather weak links.

00:13:32.100 --> 00:13:35.370
As U.S. troops are about
to raid an apartment

00:13:35.370 --> 00:13:37.917
of an uncle of a fisherman from a place

00:13:37.917 --> 00:13:42.917
where the son of the suspect
remembers fishing with his dad.

00:13:42.990 --> 00:13:45.930
And so, it comes as a
surprise to the special forces

00:13:45.930 --> 00:13:50.400
when inside the apartment
they find their suspect.

00:13:50.400 --> 00:13:54.483
Muhammad Ibrahim Omar
Al-Muslit is captured.

00:13:55.730 --> 00:13:56.880
(helicopter blades whirring)

00:13:56.880 --> 00:13:58.457
Still, there was no guarantee

00:13:58.457 --> 00:14:01.890
that Muhammad would be willing to talk.

00:14:01.890 --> 00:14:03.423
Maddox himself questions him

00:14:03.423 --> 00:14:08.070
and he offers him protection
for himself and his family.

00:14:08.070 --> 00:14:11.751
And with that assurance,
Muhammad begins to talk

00:14:11.751 --> 00:14:14.300
and he reveals that Saddam is hiding

00:14:14.300 --> 00:14:17.460
in the small farming village of Ad-Dawr,

00:14:17.460 --> 00:14:19.020
bringing us back to the scene

00:14:19.020 --> 00:14:21.243
from the very beginning of this video.

00:14:22.401 --> 00:14:24.840
As the U.S. troops searched a town,

00:14:24.840 --> 00:14:28.349
Muhammad Ibrahim is there
with them as a prisoner.

00:14:28.349 --> 00:14:30.390
Based on his information,

00:14:30.390 --> 00:14:32.430
they search two unassuming farmhouses

00:14:32.430 --> 00:14:35.460
just east of the Tigris River.

00:14:35.460 --> 00:14:37.470
But when both of them are searched,

00:14:37.470 --> 00:14:40.293
their target is still nowhere in sight.

00:14:41.336 --> 00:14:44.520
Beginning to think this
rate is just a dead end,

00:14:44.520 --> 00:14:46.954
the troops are about to give up.

00:14:46.954 --> 00:14:50.901
But then, Muhammad Ibrahim
points out another building

00:14:50.901 --> 00:14:54.840
just to the north of the second farmhouse.

00:14:54.840 --> 00:14:58.860
The building is little more
than a shack with two rooms,

00:14:58.860 --> 00:15:01.890
and no one is inside here either.

00:15:01.890 --> 00:15:04.050
It seems as though Muhammad Ibrahim

00:15:04.050 --> 00:15:06.720
has a good idea of where Saddam is,

00:15:06.720 --> 00:15:09.900
but the soldiers are not catching on.

00:15:09.900 --> 00:15:12.235
And there must have been
some final mental block

00:15:12.235 --> 00:15:14.190
that prevents Muhammad Ibrahim

00:15:14.190 --> 00:15:16.050
from straight up telling them.

00:15:16.050 --> 00:15:18.990
He is willing to help, but he
also doesn't wanna be the one

00:15:18.990 --> 00:15:21.053
giving Saddam away directly.

00:15:21.053 --> 00:15:25.680
And so, Muhammad Ibrahim begins
kicking at a piece of rope

00:15:25.680 --> 00:15:28.623
half buried in the ground outside the hut.

00:15:29.640 --> 00:15:32.049
Now, the soldiers understand.

00:15:32.049 --> 00:15:36.300
They find the trap door and Saddam.

00:15:36.300 --> 00:15:39.580
- Ladies and gentlemen, we got him.

00:15:39.580 --> 00:15:43.260
(crowd cheering and applauding)

00:15:43.260 --> 00:15:45.124
- United States military forces

00:15:45.124 --> 00:15:48.330
captured Saddam Hussein alive.

00:15:48.330 --> 00:15:52.740
In the history of Iraq, a
dark and painful era is over.

00:15:52.740 --> 00:15:55.739
A hopeful day has arrived.

00:15:55.739 --> 00:15:57.787
(screen whooshing)

00:15:57.787 --> 00:15:59.277
(somber music)

00:15:59.277 --> 00:16:02.250
- [Narrator] Even though
Saddam Hussein was captured,

00:16:02.250 --> 00:16:04.740
it didn't end the Iraq War.

00:16:04.740 --> 00:16:07.440
Coalition forces had no exit strategy

00:16:07.440 --> 00:16:09.450
once Saddam's reign had ended

00:16:09.450 --> 00:16:11.437
and instability continued for years

00:16:11.437 --> 00:16:13.654
as the country struggled to rebuild

00:16:13.654 --> 00:16:16.203
what the invasion had destroyed.

00:16:17.250 --> 00:16:19.380
The image of Saddam hiding though

00:16:19.380 --> 00:16:22.650
became one of the most iconic
ones in modern history,

00:16:22.650 --> 00:16:25.830
ingrained not just in the
timeline of global events,

00:16:25.830 --> 00:16:27.990
but also in pop culture.

00:16:27.990 --> 00:16:31.350
It even became somewhat of a
meme with people finding Saddam

00:16:31.350 --> 00:16:34.230
hiding in all kinds of random places.

00:16:34.230 --> 00:16:36.540
Wikipedia even struggled with vandalism

00:16:36.540 --> 00:16:39.907
as Saddam kept hiding in
all kinds of random graphs.

00:16:39.907 --> 00:16:42.943
But this is where it is
important to remember

00:16:42.943 --> 00:16:47.546
that this moment didn't
become iconic by itself.

00:16:47.546 --> 00:16:50.340
(gentle spirited music)

00:16:50.340 --> 00:16:52.770
After Saddam was captured in this hole,

00:16:52.770 --> 00:16:55.470
the U.S. military invited
lots of journalists

00:16:55.470 --> 00:16:57.240
to tour his hiding place,

00:16:57.240 --> 00:17:01.080
ensuring the world saw where
Saddam had been cowering.

00:17:01.080 --> 00:17:02.717
- Today, I had the chance to clamber

00:17:02.717 --> 00:17:05.280
into the tyrant's last hiding place.

00:17:05.280 --> 00:17:06.690
It's a miserable hiding place,

00:17:06.690 --> 00:17:08.220
particularly for a man who built

00:17:08.220 --> 00:17:11.151
some of the most ostentatious
palaces in the Middle East.

00:17:11.151 --> 00:17:13.860
- [Narrator] They publicized
photos of his arrest,

00:17:13.860 --> 00:17:17.460
showing him frail and utterly defeated.

00:17:17.460 --> 00:17:20.700
They also conducted a medical
examination of Saddam,

00:17:20.700 --> 00:17:22.734
where a doctor checked his teeth

00:17:22.734 --> 00:17:25.381
as though his dental hygiene was a concern

00:17:25.381 --> 00:17:27.360
after his capture.

00:17:27.360 --> 00:17:30.333
But this video also was released publicly.

00:17:31.650 --> 00:17:34.918
And really, this story isn't
just about finding Saddam.

00:17:34.918 --> 00:17:39.918
It is also a tale of the
power of different narratives.

00:17:39.960 --> 00:17:41.910
On the U.S. side, there is the narrative

00:17:41.910 --> 00:17:44.069
that there were weapons
of mass destruction

00:17:44.069 --> 00:17:47.194
later proven to be false.

00:17:47.194 --> 00:17:49.388
Both the U.S. and Saddam

00:17:49.388 --> 00:17:53.580
understood that images
can carry immense power.

00:17:53.580 --> 00:17:57.420
Saddam had spent decades
fostering a cult of personality,

00:17:57.420 --> 00:17:59.407
saturating the country with his image,

00:17:59.407 --> 00:18:01.500
using state-controlled media

00:18:01.500 --> 00:18:03.720
to build a larger than life persona

00:18:03.720 --> 00:18:08.070
while brutally oppressing
any form of opposition.

00:18:08.070 --> 00:18:12.960
And the U.S. military felt
a need to erode that myth.

00:18:12.960 --> 00:18:15.780
With the support for
the war quickly waning

00:18:15.780 --> 00:18:17.910
both in the U.S. and globally,

00:18:17.910 --> 00:18:22.260
an easy solution was to make
Saddam the face of the war.

00:18:22.260 --> 00:18:25.190
Saddam was undeniably one
of the most brutal leaders

00:18:25.190 --> 00:18:26.880
of the modern era,

00:18:26.880 --> 00:18:31.620
and the image he projected
was built on propaganda.

00:18:31.620 --> 00:18:35.370
But the carefully staged
presentation of his downfall,

00:18:35.370 --> 00:18:38.905
the fact that this very
image became so well known

00:18:38.905 --> 00:18:41.763
was no less a form of such.

00:18:42.832 --> 00:18:44.880
(gentle somber music)

00:18:44.880 --> 00:18:46.800
Telling stories like this is at the core

00:18:46.800 --> 00:18:48.870
of what I try to do with this channel.

00:18:48.870 --> 00:18:51.122
Revisiting events that shaped our world

00:18:51.122 --> 00:18:54.753
and recreating how
exactly they played out.

00:18:55.587 --> 00:18:58.860
And it is precisely what
I did for my next video,

00:18:58.860 --> 00:19:02.392
focusing on the Deep
Water Horizon catastrophe.

00:19:02.392 --> 00:19:05.580
- On April 20th, an
